cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below."
type: software
title: "HASHIRU: Hierarchical Agent System for Hybrid Intelligent Resource Utilization"
version: 2.0.0.dev0
abstract: >-
  HASHIRU is a budget-aware multi-agent system. A CEO agent splits a request into subtasks and hires manager and
  worker agents on local and cloud models, each with a dollar pool carved from its hirer's. Version 2 rebuilds it on
  open protocols: every agent is an A2A service, every tool is served over MCP, and HASHIRU itself is reachable as
  an OpenAI-compatible model, an A2A agent and an MCP server. Version 1, described in the paper, is preserved at the
  tag v1.0-paper.
